<opsproc code="00024103.0001001" revdate="2020-05-13T11:44:59"><title>RMP Key (Affected RMP Operative)</title><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00024103.0001001.001"><title>During Cockpit Preparation</title><procbody lid="N.00024103.0001001.002"><inform layer="1" lid="N.00024103.0001001.004"><unlist bulltype="NDASH" code="00024103.0001001.002" layer="1" lid="N.00024103.0001001.007"><para layer="1" lid="N.00024103.0001001.009">The flight crew shall ensure
all the following:</para><item layer="1"><para layer="1" lid="N.00024103.0001001.008"><abb>VHF</abb> 1 frequency can be changed, listen and used to contact <abb>ATC</abb>, and</para></item><item layer="1"><para layer="1" lid="N.00024103.0001001.010">If required, <abb>HF</abb> 1 frequency can be changed, listened and used to contact <abb>ATC</abb>, and</para></item><item layer="1"><para layer="1" lid="N.00024103.0001001.011"><abb>XPDR</abb> 1 can be selected, modified and be correctly received by <abb>ATC</abb> using <abb>RMP</abb> 1.</para></item></unlist></inform></procbody></procitem></opsproc>